---
// /docs/troubleshooting — common failure modes + fixes, from real gotchas: reload-gated plugin
// changes and the Node >= 24 requirement. Gotchas use .note--warn.
import DocsLayout from "../../../layouts/docs-layout/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  current="troubleshooting"
  title="Troubleshooting"
  description="Common Agentry failure modes and their fixes — plugin changes that didn't take effect, and the Node version requirement."
  eyebrow="Reference · Troubleshooting"
  lede="The handful of things that trip people up first — what you see, why it happens, and the fix. Most are a reload or a version away from working."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2 class="prose__h">Plugin changes didn't take effect</h2>
    <p>
      You edited an agent, command, skill, or MCP server, but the change isn't live in the session.
      These changes are <strong>reload-gated</strong>: they only register on a reload/restart.
    </p>
    <div class="note note--warn">
      <span class="note__key">Gotcha</span>
      <span>
        Agent / command / skill / MCP changes register only on a session restart. Restart the
        session, then verify the change live.
      </span>
    </div>

    <h2 class="prose__h">Node version errors</h2>
    <p>
      Agentry requires <strong>Node ≥ 24</strong>. The memory MCP uses <code>node:sqlite</code>, which
      isn't available on older runtimes — so an older Node fails before anything useful happens.
    </p>
    <div class="note note--warn">
      <span class="note__key">Gotcha</span>
      <span>
        Check with <code>node --version</code>. If it's below 24, upgrade Node before launching.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
